IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgh-holding-company`

-- Tests for sgh-holding-company.l4 (s 21). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the run.

§ `s 21(1) and (1A)`
-- (test alias a21a = `s 21(1) the corporation cannot be a member of the company`)
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the corporation cannot be a member of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "A corporation cannot be a member of a company which is its holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the corporation cannot be a member of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- a company that is not its holding company: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21b = `s 21(1) the allotment or transfer of the shares is void`)
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the allotment or transfer of the shares is void` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "any allotment or transfer of shares in a company to its subsidiary is void"
#ASSERT `s 21(1) the allotment or transfer of the shares is void` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- an allotment or transfer to anyone else: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21c = `s 21(1A) subsection (1) does not make the transfer void`)
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) subsection (1) does not make the transfer void` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "does not apply to a disposition of book-entry securities"
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) subsection (1) does not make the transfer void` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other transfer: the text says nothing here
-- (test alias a21d = `s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)`)
-- arguments: the Court is satisfied that a disposition of book-entry securities would be void absent (1A); the application is made by the Registrar or any other person
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "on being satisfied ... may, on the application of the Registrar or any other person, order the transfer"
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no application: a failed "on the application" gating a grant (fork line F-H-S3)
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not satisfied: a failed "on being satisfied" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
#ASSERT `s 21(1A) the Court may order the transfer of the shares acquired in contravention of subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the "on being satisfied" gate decides first

§ `s 21(2) and (3)`
-- (test alias a21e = `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary`)
-- arguments: concerned as personal representative; concerned as trustee; the holding company or a subsidiary is beneficially interested under the trust; so interested only by way of security in the ordinary course of a lending business
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "where the subsidiary is concerned as personal representative"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "or where it is concerned as trustee": not beneficially interested
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "unless the holding company or a subsidiary thereof is beneficially interested under the trust and is not so interested only by way of security"
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- interested only by way of security in a lending business: the "unless" is not met
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- as personal representative the "unless" (which follows the trustee limb) does not reach it
#ASSERT `s 21(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the subsidiary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another capacity: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21f = `s 21(3) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company`)
#ASSERT `s 21(3) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "a subsidiary which, on 29 December 1967, is a member of its holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(3) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other subsidiary: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21g = `s 21(3) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members`)
-- arguments: on 29 December 1967 a member of its holding company; subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "the subsidiary has no right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members thereof"
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "subject to subsection (2)": left to that subsection
#ASSERT `s 21(3) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other subsidiary: the text says nothing

§ `s 21(4) to (4C)`
-- (test alias a21h = `s 21(4) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company`)
#ASSERT `s 21(4) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "if, at the time when it becomes a subsidiary of the holding company, it already holds shares in that holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(4) this section does not prevent the subsidiary from continuing to be a member of its holding company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- it held no shares then: a failed "if" on an exception (fork line F-H-S3)
-- (test alias a21i = `s 21(4)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members`)
-- arguments: the (4) condition; subsection (2) applies
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(a) subject to subsection (2), the subsidiary has no right to vote"
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "subject to subsection (2)"
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the (4) condition is not met: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21j = `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares in the holding company within the period`)
-- arguments: the (4) condition; during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) ... the subsidiary must, within the period of 12 months ... dispose of all of its shares in the holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (4A): "ceases to apply if, during the period ..., the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the (4) condition is not met: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21k = `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares`)
-- arguments: the date it became a subsidiary; the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if any
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` (Date 15 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 15 3 2027   -- "within the period of 12 months": 15 March 2026 plus 12 months (P4)
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` (Date 15 3 2026) (JUST (Date 30 9 2027)) EQUALS Date 30 9 2027   -- "or such longer period as the Court may allow": the later day
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` (Date 15 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027   -- an earlier day is not "longer": 12 months stands
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of its shares` (Date 29 2 2024) NOTHING EQUALS Date 28 2 2025   -- 29 February 2024 plus 12 months ends on the last day of February (P4)
-- (test alias a21l = `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period`)
-- arguments: the date it became a subsidiary; the last day of the longer period allowed, if any; the date it disposed of all its shares
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 15 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of the 12 months
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 15 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 15 3 2026) (JUST (Date 30 9 2027)) (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the longer period the Court allowed
#ASSERT `s 21(4)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of its shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 15 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before it became a subsidiary: outside "after becoming"
-- (test alias a21m = `s 21(4A) subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply`)
#ASSERT `s 21(4A) subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "ceases to apply if, during the period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(4A) subsection (4)(b) ceases to apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no other way is stated
-- (test alias a21n = `s 21(4B) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares`)
-- arguments: the shares are not disposed of in accordance with (4)(b); subsections (4C) and (6E) are complied with
#ASSERT `s 21(4B) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Any shares ... that are not disposed of in accordance with subsection (4)(b) may, subject to subsections (4C) and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary"
#ASSERT `s 21(4B) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "subject to" (4C) and (6E): the text says nothing (fork line F-H-S3)
#ASSERT `s 21(4B) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- shares disposed of: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21o = `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as`)
-- arguments: the shares are shares referred to in (4B); the reference
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(4C)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to shares referred to in subsection (4B)"   -- "(i) a reference to treasury shares is a reference to shares referred to in subsection (4B)"
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(4C)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in subsection (4B)"   -- "(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares is a reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in subsection (4B)"
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(4C)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied` EQUALS JUST "as if they were already held by the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(4) applied"   -- "(iii) ... is a reference to 'as if they were already held by the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(4) applied'"
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(4C) another reference in sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "including the following modifications": the others are not stated (includes)
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(a) the reference is read as` FALSE `s 21(4C)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- other shares: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21p = `s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time`)
-- arguments: the date of the change in the number of shares; the date the notice was lodged
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 14 days after any change": 1 May plus 14 days is 15 May
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of the change is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 16 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late: a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 21(4C)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the change: not "after" it

§ `s 21(5) and (6)`
-- (test alias a21q = `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary`)
-- arguments: the subsection; the person is a nominee for a corporation which is a subsidiary; subsection (2) applies to the subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "subsections (1), (3), (4), (4B), (6A) and (6C) apply in relation to a nominee"
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (3)
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (4)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (4)
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (4B)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (4B)
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (6A)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (6A)
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (6C)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (6C)
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) another subsection` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another subsection: the text does not say "only"
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "Subject to subsection (2)": left to that subsection
#ASSERT `s 21(5) the subsection applies in relation to the nominee as it applies to the subsidiary` `s 21(5) subsection (1)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not a nominee: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21r = `s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary`)
-- arguments: the subsidiary already lawfully holds shares; by capitalisation of reserves; to all members in direct proportion to the shares each holds
#ASSERT `s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "if the allotment is made by way of capitalisation of reserves ... and is made to all members ... in direct proportion"
#ASSERT `s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- the subsidiary held no shares lawfully: a failed "if" on an exception (fork line F-H-S3)
#ASSERT `s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not by capitalisation of reserves
#ASSERT `s 21(6) this section does not operate to prevent the allotment of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not in direct proportion

§ `s 21(6A) to (6D)`
-- (test alias a21s = `s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` `s 21(6A) a distribution in specie` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "by way of a distribution in specie"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` `s 21(6A) an amalgamation` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "amalgamation"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` `s 21(6A) a scheme of arrangement` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "scheme of arrangement"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A) this section does not operate to prevent the transfer of shares in the holding company to the subsidiary` `s 21(6A) another way of transfer` EQUALS NOTHING   -- the list does not say "only"
-- (test alias a21t = `s 21(6A)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members`)
-- arguments: transferred by one of the three ways; subsection (2) applies
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(a) subject to subsection (2), the subsidiary has no right to vote"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- "subject to subsection (2)"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(a) the subsidiary has a right to vote at meetings of the holding company or any class of members` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another way of transfer: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21u = `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares in the holding company within the period`)
-- arguments: transferred by one of the three ways; during the period the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) ... the subsidiary must, within the period of 12 months ... dispose of all of the shares"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- (6B): "ceases to apply if, during the period ..., the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary"
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- another way of transfer: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21v = `s 21(6A)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares`)
-- arguments: the date the shares were transferred to the subsidiary; the last day of the longer period the Court allowed, if any
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares` (Date 30 6 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 30 6 2027   -- "within the period of 12 months": 30 June 2026 plus 12 months
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the last day of the period within which the subsidiary must dispose of all of the shares` (Date 30 6 2026) (JUST (Date 31 12 2027)) EQUALS Date 31 12 2027   -- the longer period the Court allowed
-- (test alias a21w = `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company within the period`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 30 6 2026) NOTHING (Date 30 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the last day of the 12 months
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 30 6 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 21(6A)(b) the subsidiary disposed of all of the shares in the holding company within the period` (Date 30 6 2026) (JUST (Date 31 12 2027)) (Date 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the longer period
-- (test alias a21x = `s 21(6B) subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6B) subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "ceases to apply if, during the period referred to in that subsection, the subsidiary ceases to be a subsidiary of the holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(6B) subsection (6A)(b) ceases to apply` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no other way is stated
-- (test alias a21y = `s 21(6C) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6C) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "may, subject to subsections (6D) and (6E), be held or continued to be held by the subsidiary"
#ASSERT `s 21(6C) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not "subject to" (6D) and (6E) (fork line F-H-S3)
#ASSERT `s 21(6C) the subsidiary may hold or continue to hold the shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- shares disposed of: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21z = `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(6D)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to shares referred to in subsection (6C)"   -- "(i) a reference to treasury shares is a reference to shares referred to in subsection (6C)"
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(6D)(a)(ii) a reference to a company holding treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to a subsidiary holding shares referred to in subsection (6C)"   -- "(ii)"
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(6D)(a)(iii) the reference in section 76J(6) to the purchase of the shares by the company at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 76H applied` EQUALS JUST "as if they were transferred to the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(6A) applied"   -- "(iii) ... a reference to 'as if they were transferred to the subsidiary at the time they were allotted, in circumstances in which section 21(6A) applied'"
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` TRUE `s 21(6D) another reference in sections 76J(1), (2), (3), (5) and (6) and 76K` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "including the following modifications": the others are not stated (includes)
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(a) the reference is read as` FALSE `s 21(6D)(a)(i) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- other shares: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21aa = `s 21(6D)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 14 days after any change": 1 May plus 14 days is 15 May
#ASSERT `s 21(6D)(b) the holding company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 16 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late (periods ruling (a))

§ `s 21(6E) and (6F)`
-- (test alias a21ab = `s 21(6E)(a) the aggregate number of shares exceeds 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company`)
-- arguments: shares of only one class; the aggregate number held; the total number of shares
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(a) the aggregate number of shares exceeds 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company` TRUE 100 1000 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "must not at any time exceed 10%": exactly 10% is not over
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(a) the aggregate number of shares exceeds 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company` TRUE 101 1000 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one share over 10%
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(a) the aggregate number of shares exceeds 10% of the total number of shares of the holding company` FALSE 500 1000 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(a) where the holding company has shares of only one class": a failed "where" (periods ruling (b)); paragraph (b) governs
-- (test alias a21ac = `s 21(6E)(b) the aggregate number of the shares of the class exceeds 10% of the total number of the shares in that class`)
-- arguments: shares of different classes; the aggregate number of the class held; the total number of the shares in that class
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(b) the aggregate number of the shares of the class exceeds 10% of the total number of the shares in that class` TRUE 100 1000 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- exactly 10% of the class is not over
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(b) the aggregate number of the shares of the class exceeds 10% of the total number of the shares in that class` TRUE 101 1000 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one share over 10% of the class
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(b) the aggregate number of the shares of the class exceeds 10% of the total number of the shares in that class` FALSE 500 1000 EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(b) where the share capital ... is divided into shares of different classes": a failed "where" (periods ruling (b)); paragraph (a) governs
-- (test alias a21ad = `s 21(6E)(c) the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "where paragraph (a) or (b) is contravened, the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares"
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the holding company must dispose of or cancel the excess shares, or procure the disposal of the excess shares by its subsidiary` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no contravention: a duty whose "where" gate is unmet (marginal reading (a))
-- (test alias a21ae = `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares`)
-- arguments: the day on which the contravention occurs; the last day of the further period the Registrar allowed, if any
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 30 6 2026   -- "the period of 6 months beginning with the day on which that contravention occurs": 1 January is day 1 (P10), so the period ends on 30 June
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 31 7 2026)) EQUALS Date 31 7 2026   -- "or such further period as the Registrar may allow"
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 15 6 2026)) EQUALS Date 30 6 2026   -- an earlier day is not "further": 6 months stands
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the last day of the period for disposing of or cancelling the excess shares` (Date 31 8 2026) NOTHING EQUALS Date 28 2 2027   -- beginning on 31 August, the 6 months end on 28 February (P4 clamp, P10)
-- (test alias a21af = `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time`)
-- arguments: the day of the contravention; the last day of the further period allowed, if any; the day the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled; the disposal was in accordance with section 76K
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "before the end of the period of 6 months ..., in accordance with section 76K": the last day
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day later (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not "in accordance with section 76K"
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 31 7 2026)) (Date 15 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- inside the further period the Registrar allowed
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(c) the excess shares were disposed of or cancelled in time` (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- before the contravention: outside the period
-- (test alias a21ag = `s 21(6E)(d) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares`)
-- arguments: the shares are shares referred to in (4B) or (6C); the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(d) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "(d) where the subsidiary is a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company, no dividend may be paid, and no other distribution ... may be made"
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(d) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not wholly-owned: paragraph (e) is the question for that case
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(d) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other shares: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21ah = `s 21(6E)(e) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares`)
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(e) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(e) where the subsidiary is not a wholly-owned subsidiary of the holding company, a dividend may be paid and other distribution ... may be made"
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(e) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- a wholly-owned subsidiary: a failed "where" on a "may" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii)); paragraph (d) says no
#ASSERT `s 21(6E)(e) a dividend or other distribution of the holding company's assets may be paid or made to the subsidiary in respect of the shares` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- other shares: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21ai = `s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares`)
-- arguments: the aggregate number held; the total number of shares
#ASSERT `s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares` 101 1005 EQUALS 1   -- 10% of 1,005 is 100.5, so 100 shares are within the limit and 101 held is 1 over
#ASSERT `s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares` 100 1005 EQUALS 0   -- within the limit: no excess
#ASSERT `s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares` 150 1000 EQUALS 50   -- 10% of 1,000 is 100; 150 held is 50 over
#ASSERT `s 21(6F) "excess shares" the number of excess shares` 0 0 EQUALS 0   -- no shares: no excess

§ `s 21(6G) to (9)`
#ASSERT count `s 21(6G) the sections in which the references are read as stated` EQUALS 20   -- the text lists 20 provisions: 7(9)(ca), 33(5A), 63A(1)(e), 74(1A), 76B(3E), 78, 81(4), 164A(1), 176(1A), 177(1), 179(8), 184(4)(b)(i), 201A(4)(b), 205B(6), 206(1)(b), 215(1), (1C), (1D) and (3A), 232(1)(a)(i)
-- (test alias a21aj = `s 21(6G) the reference includes`)
-- arguments: the section; the kind of reference
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "78" `s 21(6G)(a) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to shares held by a subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C)"   -- "(a) a reference to 'treasury shares' includes a reference to shares held by a subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C)"
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "232(1)(a)(i)" `s 21(6G)(b) a reference to a company being registered as a member of itself or being a member of itself` EQUALS JUST "a reference to a subsidiary being registered as a member of its holding company"   -- "(b) ... includes a reference to a subsidiary being registered as a member of its holding company"
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "215(1D)" `s 21(6G)(a) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to shares held by a subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C)"   -- "215(1), (1C), (1D) and (3A)": the third of the four
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "7(9)(ca)" `s 21(6G)(a) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS JUST "a reference to shares held by a subsidiary under subsection (4B) or (6C)"   -- the first listed
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "76J" `s 21(6G)(a) a reference to treasury shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a section not listed: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 21(6G) the reference includes` "78" `s 21(6G) another reference` EQUALS NOTHING   -- another kind of reference: the text says nothing
-- (test alias a21ak = `s 21(7) the holding company may on behalf of the subsidiary sell the shares for which the subsidiary would otherwise have been entitled to subscribe`)
#ASSERT `s 21(7) the holding company may on behalf of the subsidiary sell the shares for which the subsidiary would otherwise have been entitled to subscribe` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "Where but for this section a subsidiary would have been entitled to subscribe for shares in the holding company, the holding company may, on behalf of the subsidiary, sell the shares"
#ASSERT `s 21(7) the holding company may on behalf of the subsidiary sell the shares for which the subsidiary would otherwise have been entitled to subscribe` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- no such entitlement: a failed "where" on a "may" (periods ruling (b); split site (ii))
-- (test alias a21al = `s 21(8) the reference to shares in this section includes a reference to the interest of the members as such, whatever the form of that interest`)
#ASSERT `s 21(8) the reference to shares in this section includes a reference to the interest of the members as such, whatever the form of that interest` `limited by guarantee` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "In relation to a holding company that is a company limited by guarantee"
#ASSERT `s 21(8) the reference to shares in this section includes a reference to the interest of the members as such, whatever the form of that interest` `limited by shares` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other holding company: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 21(8) the reference to shares in this section includes a reference to the interest of the members as such, whatever the form of that interest` `unlimited` EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other holding company: the text says nothing
#ASSERT `s 21(8) the reference to shares in this section includes a reference to the interest of the members as such, whatever the form of that interest` `limited by shares and by guarantee` EQUALS NOTHING   -- a company limited both by shares and by guarantee is not named
-- (test alias a21am = `s 21(9) the company must inform the Registrar of the occurrence of the event by lodging a notice in the prescribed form`)
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company must inform the Registrar of the occurrence of the event by lodging a notice in the prescribed form` `s 21(9)(a) a shareholder of a company that is a corporation becomes a subsidiary of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(a) where a shareholder of a company that is a corporation becomes a subsidiary of the company"
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company must inform the Registrar of the occurrence of the event by lodging a notice in the prescribed form` `s 21(9)(b) shares of the company are held by a subsidiary of the company and there is a change in the number of shares held by the subsidiary` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "(b) where shares of the company are held by a subsidiary of the company and there is a change in the number of shares held by the subsidiary"
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company must inform the Registrar of the occurrence of the event by lodging a notice in the prescribed form` `s 21(9) another event` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "any of the following events": the text does not say "only"
-- (test alias a21an = `s 21(9) the company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time`)
-- arguments: the event; the date of occurrence; the date the notice was lodged
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` `s 21(9)(a) a shareholder of a company that is a corporation becomes a subsidiary of the company` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- "within 14 days after the date of occurrence": 1 May plus 14 days is 15 May
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` `s 21(9)(a) a shareholder of a company that is a corporation becomes a subsidiary of the company` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 16 5 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- one day late (periods ruling (a))
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` `s 21(9)(b) shares of the company are held by a subsidiary of the company and there is a change in the number of shares held by the subsidiary` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day of occurrence is in time (fork line F-H-P2)
#ASSERT `s 21(9) the company lodged the notice with the Registrar in time` `s 21(9) another event` (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 15 5 2026) EQUALS NOTHING   -- another event: the text says nothing

§ `Regulative rules of s 21`
-- A BREACH path exists for each: the act at the last day reads FULFILLED, one day later BREACH, no act by then BREACH, and no act at all RESIDUAL.
-- s 21(4)(b): 12 months (365 days from 15 March 2026 to 15 March 2027).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 21(4)(b) rule: the subsidiary's duty to dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` (Company "Sub Pte Ltd") 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Sub Pte Ltd" DOES `s 21(4)(b) dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` AT 365
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 21(4)(b) rule: the subsidiary's duty to dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` (Company "Sub Pte Ltd") 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Sub Pte Ltd" DOES `s 21(4)(b) dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` AT 366
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 21(4)(b) rule: the subsidiary's duty to dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` (Company "Sub Pte Ltd") 365 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAITUNTIL` 366)
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 21(4)(b) rule: the subsidiary's duty to dispose of all of its shares in the holding company` (Company "Sub Pte Ltd") 365 AT 0 WITH
